    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0885" n="867" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20210/5–346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Shaw</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-03T18:00:00-05:00">May 3, 1946—6 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 4—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>231. Reurtel April 30, 8 a.m.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d736-f1"/> Only German school
                    in Ecuador Colegio Leman of Quito was closed and German instructors returned to
                    Germany April 1942. Suspected successor school Penjionado Gonzalez Suarez closed
                    July 1943 by inclusion on PL.</p>
                <p>Official German propaganda continued clandestinely by Max Rueff in charge of
                    German affairs at Spanish Legation after Eucador broke relations in January 1942
                    continued until November 1943 when Rueff arrested and interned in US.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shaw</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d736-f1" n="64" xml:id="d736-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; in it the Department requested reports on the liquidation of German
                    schools and other propaganda and cultural agencies (862.20210/4–3046).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
